 {
  "kind": "text",
  "text": "I built the Pulse sting on the 8 s timeline, locked to the 120 BPM grid. I only checked it in a contact sheet of stills (3.5 s to 7.5 s). I didn't run `critique` or play it back with the music.\n\n- **Build, 0–4 s:** The teal **dot** fades in and pulses on every beat, getting bigger each time. The white **ring** fades up from 2 s and swells toward the drop. At 3.5 s the dot shrinks hard, so the 0.5 s before the drop feels held back.\n- **Drop, 4.0 s:** The ring snaps to full size on the downbeat, the dot pops back, and a **shock** ring bursts outward from the mark.\n- **After the drop:**\n  - At 4.5 s the mark slides left.\n  - At 4.7 s the **word** \"Pulse\" slides in beside it.\n  - The beat at 5.5 s gets a pulse on the ring and dot plus a second shock ring, and the lockup settles by about 6.2 s.\n  - The lockup then holds clean until the end.\n\nThe mark and wordmark are centered as one lockup. If you'd like it bouncier or more minimal, I can retune the easing. I can also add sound effects.",
  "at": 1794511106094
 },
